diag: the TOP lines also say how much of each process's CPU time is spent inside the kernel (0360)

min35 (E-0256): backboardd shows 128 % of a core on average and up to 615 %, yet in 809 thread samples (every 2 s) only 13 were outside the kernel's wait calls: the sampler reads the saved context of a thread, which is stale for one that is running, so it cannot profile CPU-bound threads. TOP lines gain a system-time field (' name 128% s90'): if most of backboardd's time is system time it is spent in traps and IOKit calls (the HeroGPU submit polls for the job's end), not in drawing code. sweet_sample.c only; the report tool parses the first number as before.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c
